  "title": "Writing chords down",
  "summary": "The short names on a band chart: C means C major, Cm means C minor.",
  "minutes": 5,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Chord symbol",
      "body": "Band charts name chords with a **chord symbol**: the root letter, plus a short tag for the kind of chord. A letter on its own means major: **C** is C major. A small **m** means minor: **Cm** is C minor.\n\n**Why it matters:** This is how bands write songs down. A chart is a row of chord symbols over the lyrics, and you play each one as you reach it.",
